course: dictionary
lesson: 6668
title: Oasis: water in a dry place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a word from the words around it. This is its context. «Traders travelled in caravans of camels across the deserts, resting in oasis towns.» Deserts, camels and resting are the clues, so an oasis is a place where travellers can stop.
explain: «These lands are mostly dry, so people built cities where water is.» The clue is water: an oasis is where water is in a dry place. Check your idea by swapping it in. "People built cities at water places along the Silk Road" still makes sense.
explain: Oasis also has a figurative meaning, a calm, pleasant place in the middle of a busy or difficult place. «A quiet library can be an oasis of calm.» A library is not a desert, so here it means a peaceful place inside a noisy world.
explain: Keep the picture of water and palm trees in mind. Real oases are in deserts. The word also has the calm sense, so read the sentence to see which one fits.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Oasis» means a place in a desert where there is water, so plants and trees such as date palms can grow.
fact: An «oasis» is a place where underground water reaches the surface or can be dug out easily.
fact: Cities such as Samarkand, Bukhara and Kashgar grew rich at oases on the Silk Road.
fact: «An oasis of calm» means a calm, pleasant place in the middle of a busy or difficult place.
exercise: «Traders rested in oasis towns across the deserts.» What is an oasis? | A road that crosses the mountains | A very large sandy hill with no water at all | A type of camel with two humps | *A place in a desert where there is water, so plants and trees can grow
exercise: «An oasis is a place in a desert where underground water reaches the surface, so palms and crops can grow.» Find and copy the one word that tells you what an oasis needs. | desert | palms | *water | crops
exercise: «A quiet library can be an oasis of calm.» What does oasis mean here? | A place with no water and no plants | *A calm, pleasant place in the middle of a busy place | A loud, busy shop | A library full of sand
test: «Caravans of camels crossed the desert from one oasis to the next.» Why would the travellers stop at oases? | *To drink and rest | To count the grains of sand | To climb the mountains | To sing to the camels
test: Ella says an oasis is always a shop. What does the dictionary say? | A type of camel | A road made of stone | A shop in the middle of a desert | *A place in a desert where there is water, or a calm place in a busy one
exam: Which sentence uses oasis in the calm, figurative sense? | «The camels drank deeply from the oasis pool.» | «The caravan rested at the oasis, where date palms grew.» | «Oases are found in deserts where water is near the surface.» | *«The quiet garden was an oasis after the noisy street.»
